[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128243,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Atypical intradermal smooth muscle neoplasm is a primary dermal neoplasm composed of generally well-differentiated spindled cells closely resembling normal arrector pili smooth muscle but showing nuclear enlargement, hyperchromatism, and mitotic activity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128244,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8897/1 Atypical intradermal smooth muscle neoplasm</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128245,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F9C &amp; XH1EN1 Neoplasms of unknown behaviour of connective or other soft tissue &amp; Smooth muscle tumour of uncertain malignant potential</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128246,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> cutaneous leiomyosarcoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> pilar leiomyosarcoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128247,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128248,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours most commonly involve the trunk and lower extremities {21358302; 20102404}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128249,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours typically manifest as small (5&ndash;30&nbsp;mm), solitary, and occasionally painful nodules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128250,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cutaneous leiomyosarcomas are rare, with an age-adjusted incidence of roughly 0.2&nbsp;cases&nbsp;per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;person-years {31729020}. They most often occur in older men, with a mean patient age of 56&nbsp;years and an M:F&nbsp;ratio of 3:1 to 4:1 {21358302; 20102404}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128251,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rare cases have been described in association with Li&ndash;Fraumeni syndrome {21358302}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128252,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The genetic events underlying the development of atypical intradermal smooth muscle neoplasm are unknown. Germline <em>FH</em> mutation does not appear to be a predisposing factor {20618355}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128253,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128254,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Atypical intradermal smooth muscle neoplasms are typically well differentiated, consisting of fascicles of relatively uniform, eosinophilic spindled cells with perinuclear vacuoles and cigar-shaped nuclei. Compared with normal pilar smooth muscle, these tumours show greater cellularity, nuclear enlargement, and hyperchromatism, and they show mitotic activity.</p>\r\n<p>Marked nuclear pleomorphism and necrosis are rare; the presence of such features should raise concern for metastasis from a deeply situated tumour, which may be regarded as cutaneous leiomyosarcoma {21989966}. Atypical intradermal smooth muscle neoplasms typically grow in an infiltrative fashion into the surrounding dermis, and they may show limited involvement of the subcutaneous fat.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemically, these tumours are essentially always positive for SMA and desmin, and almost always positive for caldesmon {21358302; 20102404}. Expression of keratins may be seen in as many as 45% of cases {21358302}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128255,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128256,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128257,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a dermal-based tumour with an infiltrative growth pattern; fascicles of relatively uniform, eosinophilic spindled cells with perinuclear vacuoles and cigar-shaped nuclei; variable SMA, desmin, and caldesmon expression; limited involvement of the subcutaneous fat.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128258,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 128259,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 279,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis of these tumours is excellent, with no metastases documented in the largest series to date (84&nbsp;cases) for tumours confined to the dermis that are completely excised {21358302}. Data are limited, but dermal tumours showing subcutaneous involvement may have a low risk of metastasis and recurrence. Grading is not of prognostic value.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T14:39:30"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]